// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
/// @file
/// Documentation of the namespaces that enclose the libraries and the desktop application.
///
/// These namespaces are opened in many files and have no header of their own, so they are
/// documented here, once. Every nested namespace is documented in the header that declares
/// its central type (see docs/development/coding-standards.md).

/// @namespace nmeasim
/// Everything in NMEA Simulator X: the `core` and `io` libraries, the desktop application
/// and the test helpers.
///
/// The command-line tool keeps its code in an anonymous namespace of `src/cli/main.cpp`.

/// @namespace nmeasim::core
/// The simulation engine, a static library with no Qt dependency (CMake target
/// `nmeasim::core`).
///
/// It models the vessel (`model`), produces its state over time (`simulation`), and encodes
/// that state as NMEA 0183 sentences (`nmea0183`), AIS messages (`ais`), Signal K deltas
/// (`signalk`) and ViewSync packets (`viewsync`). It also reads tracks (`track`) and log
/// files (`log`). Nothing in it blocks, sleeps or performs network or serial I/O, so every
/// part can be tested in isolation and driven by any host.

/// @namespace nmeasim::io
/// Profiles, transports and the simulation runner: a static library on Qt Core, Network,
/// Serial Port and WebSockets (CMake target `nmeasim::io`).
///
/// A `Profile` is the persistent description of a simulation and its outputs;
/// `SimulationRunner` drives a `core::simulation::Simulation` on a Qt timer and writes what
/// it produces to `Transport` implementations. Both the desktop application and the
/// command-line tool are built on it.

/// @namespace nmeasim::app
/// The Qt Widgets desktop application: the main window, its dock panels, the map, the
/// instruments and the settings dialog, built on `nmeasim::io`.
